# Manual requests (REST Client). Run npm run seed first; send in order.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000
@tenantA = aaaaaaaa-aaaa-4aaa-8aaa-aaaaaaaaaaaa
@tenantB = bbbbbbbb-bbbb-4bbb-8bbb-bbbbbbbbbbbb

#######################################################################
# Email ingestion
#######################################################################

### 1. A new email for Tenant A opens a case (201, created_case: true)
# @name firstEmail
POST {{baseUrl}}/emails
x-tenant-id: {{tenantA}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "message_id": "<heating-1@mail.example.com>",
  "in_reply_to": null,
  "from": "resident@example.com",
  "subject": "Heating is broken in flat 4B",
  "body": "No heating since this morning."
}

### 2. A reply joins the same case (201, created_case: false, same case_id)
POST {{baseUrl}}/emails
x-tenant-id: {{tenantA}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "message_id": "<heating-2@mail.example.com>",
  "in_reply_to": "<heating-1@mail.example.com>",
  "from": "resident@example.com",
  "subject": "Re: Heating is broken in flat 4B",
  "body": "Still cold."
}

### 3. The same email again is ignored (200, duplicate: true)
POST {{baseUrl}}/emails
x-tenant-id: {{tenantA}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "message_id": "<heating-2@mail.example.com>",
  "in_reply_to": "<heating-1@mail.example.com>",
  "from": "resident@example.com",
  "subject": "Re: Heating is broken in flat 4B",
  "body": "Still cold."
}

### 4. The thread of the case: both emails, oldest first
GET {{baseUrl}}/cases/{{firstEmail.response.body.case_id}}/emails
x-tenant-id: {{tenantA}}

### 5. ISOLATION: Tenant B replies to Tenant A's message_id -> B gets its own new case (created_case: true)
POST {{baseUrl}}/emails
x-tenant-id: {{tenantB}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "message_id": "<forged-reply@mail.example.com>",
  "in_reply_to": "<heating-1@mail.example.com>",
  "from": "intruder@example.com",
  "subject": "Re: Heating is broken in flat 4B",
  "body": "Trying to join someone else's thread."
}

### 6. ISOLATION: Tenant B reads the thread of Tenant A's case (404)
GET {{baseUrl}}/cases/{{firstEmail.response.body.case_id}}/emails
x-tenant-id: {{tenantB}}

### 7. Invalid email: missing message_id, bad from (400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/emails
x-tenant-id: {{tenantA}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "from": "not an address",
  "subject": "x",
  "body": "x"
}

#######################################################################
# Cases
#######################################################################

### 8. Tenant A lists its cases
GET {{baseUrl}}/cases
x-tenant-id: {{tenantA}}

### 9. Tenant B lists its cases (only the one from request 5)
GET {{baseUrl}}/cases
x-tenant-id: {{tenantB}}

### 10. ISOLATION: Tenant B reads Tenant A's case (404)
GET {{baseUrl}}/cases/{{firstEmail.response.body.case_id}}
x-tenant-id: {{tenantB}}

### 11. ISOLATION: Tenant B closes Tenant A's case (404)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/cases/{{firstEmail.response.body.case_id}}/status
x-tenant-id: {{tenantB}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "closed"
}

### 12. Tenant A closes its own case (200)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/cases/{{firstEmail.response.body.case_id}}/status
x-tenant-id: {{tenantA}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "closed"
}

### 13. No tenant header (401)
GET {{baseUrl}}/cases
